<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="ai_tech_competition::automation_adoption_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased kinetic combat and personnel losses create urgent operational gaps that accelerate fielding and adoption of autonomous sensors, logistics drones and AI decision aids to substitute for or protect human forces, raising the rate of automation deployment.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_tech_competition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="energy_geopolitics_shift::supply_disruption_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased kinetic strikes against pipelines, terminals and transport corridors physically damage energy infrastructure and logistics, directly raising the likelihood and severity of upstream and midstream supply disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_geopolitics_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="monetary_bond_stress::portfolio_flow_volumes" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in kinetic attack intensity prompt flight-to-safety and rapid risk‑off rebalancing, driving large net inflows into core government bonds and outflows from equities and risk assets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">monetary_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_attack_intensity" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::market_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained, high-intensity Russian strikes raise near-term tail‑risk perceptions for global energy and trade, causing investors and insurers to demand higher risk premia on Gulf‑linked assets and financings.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
