<edge source="monetary_bond_stress::long_term_bond_yields" target="ai_tech_competition::investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher long-term yields increase discount rates and the effective cost of financing capital-intensive AI projects (data centers, GPUs), prompting institutional and venture investors to scale back or reprice commitments to AI infrastructure and R&amp;D.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_tech_competition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_bond_stress::long_term_bond_yields" target="energy_geopolitics_shift::oil_production_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising long-term government bond yields increase discount rates and the cost of project financing for capital‑intensive upstream oil investments, causing firms to defer or cancel capacity expansion and thus reduce near‑term production capability.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_geopolitics_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_bond_stress::long_term_bond_yields" target="russia_ukraine_war::supply_chain_integrity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher long-term yields increase the cost of capital for defense contractors and their suppliers, leading firms to cut inventory, delay investment and subcontracting, which degrades the reliability and continuity of defense-relevant supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_bond_stress::long_term_bond_yields" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::oil_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in long-term yields raises global discount rates and signals weaker near-term growth, reducing expected oil demand and putting downward pressure on benchmark crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
