<edge source="monetary_bond_stress::portfolio_flow_volumes" target="ai_tech_competition::market_concentration" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained reallocation of portfolio flows out of risk assets into safe bonds reduces liquidity and follow-on funding for smaller AI startups, increasing exits, distress sales and acquisition opportunities that consolidate customers and infrastructure among a few well-capitalized incumbents.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_tech_competition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_bond_stress::portfolio_flow_volumes" target="energy_geopolitics_shift::control_over_reserves" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising cross‑border portfolio inflows provide foreign energy firms and funds with liquidity to acquire equity stakes or finance takeovers of oil assets, increasing external actors' operational or proprietary control over reserves.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_geopolitics_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_bond_stress::portfolio_flow_volumes" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Larger net portfolio inflows into allied markets relieve fiscal and currency stress and sustain domestic political support for external military assistance, whereas rapid outflows (the inverse) increase domestic pressure to reduce foreign aid and thereby weaken political‑military cohesion among allies.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="monetary_bond_stress::portfolio_flow_volumes" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::oil_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Large net portfolio outflows from risk assets into safe assets depress growth and commodity demand expectations and trigger selling in commodity-linked positions, lowering oil prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">monetary_bond_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
