  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">An increased probability of upstream or transit disruptions is incorporated into markets as a higher near-term supply risk premium, directly lifting benchmark crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_geopolitics_shift</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
